message.content:
This is a CBP ruling-type item. An air separator for hydronic systems with an automatic air vent is probably classified as a filtering/purifying machine or as a valve. Past CBP rulings on Caleffi air separators (e.g., NY N0xx) classified them in 8421.29 (filtering or purifying machinery for liquids, other) or in 8481.80. Air/dirt separators have been classified in 8421.29.0065 ("Other: Other"). The device removes gas from liquid by coalescence, which is a purifying function, so I'm going with 8421.29.0065.

The HTS lists 8421.29.00 with these subdivisions: 8421.29.0005 (Dialysis), 8421.29.0020 (Of a kind used for filtering or purifying beverages), 8421.29.0030 (Oil filters), 8421.29.0050 (Other: Filtering/purifying machinery for water), and 8421.29.0065 (Other). That gives 8421.29.0065 for this item.

{"hts_code": "8421.29.0065", "reason": "The air separator purifies hydronic system fluid by removing entrained air through coalescence, making it filtering or purifying machinery for liquids, other (8421.29), rather than a mere valve."}
